-- Everything the language knows about numbers.

-- The two constants, written out so that nobody who remembers a value under one of
-- those names is quietly overruled.
please show the number pi rounded to 5 decimal places
please show the number e rounded to 5 decimal places

-- Trigonometry. Angles are in radians, the way mathematics does it.
please show the sine of the number pi divided by 2
please show the cosine of 0
please show the tangent of 0
please show the angle whose sine is 1
please show the angle whose cosine is 1
please show the angle whose tangent is 0
please show the angle of 1 over 1

-- Turning one kind of angle into the other.
please show 180 in radians rounded to 5 decimal places
please show the number pi in degrees
please show (the sine of 30 in radians) rounded to 4 decimal places

-- The hyperbolic ones, for hanging chains and for growth.
please show the hyperbolic sine of 0
please show the hyperbolic cosine of 0
please show the hyperbolic tangent of 0

-- Logarithms, and their undoing.
please show the natural logarithm of the number e or 0
please show the common logarithm of 1000
please show the logarithm of 8 in base 2
please show the exponential of 0
please show the exponential of 1 rounded to 5 decimal places

-- Powers and roots.
please show 7 squared
please show 3 cubed
please show 2.5 squared
please show the cube root of 27
please show the square root of 81

-- Taking a number apart.
please show the whole part of 3.7
please show the fraction part of 3.5
please show the sign of 0 minus 12
please show the sign of 12
please show the sign of 0
please show 3.14159 rounded to 2 decimal places

-- Keeping a number where you want it. Keeping something between two ends is said about the
-- whole sum, so it does not need brackets to reach across the arithmetic.
please show 15 kept between 1 and 10
please show 0 minus 5 kept between 1 and 10
please show 5 kept between 1 and 10
please show 3 plus 40 kept between 1 and 10

-- Squaring, on the other hand, belongs to the number right beside it.
please show 2 plus 3 squared
please show (2 plus 3) squared

-- Whole numbers, the way school teaches them.
please show the greatest common factor of 12 and 18
please show the smallest common multiple of 4 and 6
please show the factorial of 10
please show the factorial of 21 or 0
please show the remainder of 17 divided by 5

-- Statistics.
please remember marks is an empty list
please for every m in the pieces of "2 4 4 4 5 5 7 9" split by " ":
    add the number in m or 0 to marks
thanks

please show "average {the average of marks or 0}"
please show "median {the median of marks or 0}"
please show "spread {the spread of marks or 0}"
please show "biggest {the biggest of marks or 0}"
please show "smallest {the smallest of marks or 0}"

-- Percentages, both ways round.
please show 25 as a percentage of 200
please show 15 percent of 200

-- And the ones that cannot work out say so, rather than inventing an answer.
please show the angle whose sine is 2 or 0 minus 1
please show the natural logarithm of 0 or 0 minus 1
please show 5 as a percentage of 0 or 0 minus 1

please try to:
    show the factorial of 30
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "as expected: {what went wrong}"
thank you for trying
